# C1-S03 — A Normal Afternoon. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1626–1652.
# There's no alarm for about five minutes of play. The village has to feel lived
# in before anything threatens it. Each node is one NPC or moment; the
# farmers' argument sets up the uphill water in C1-S05, and the child sets up
# "Uncle Aldric" in C1-S08.

~ chicken
Child: Mum! There's two Pebbles!
Mother: There's one Pebbles, love.
do chicken_duplicate
Kaelen: ...
Kaelen: I'm not going to ask about the chicken.

~ old_fen
Old Fen: New, are you.
Kaelen: I guess so.
Old Fen: You'll get over it.
Kaelen: Being new?
Old Fen: Guessing.

~ jessa
Jessa: Elara brought you in?
Kaelen: Is that unusual?
Jessa: She usually brings in plants.
Kaelen: Better company, probably.
Jessa: Quieter. Plants don't ask where the crater went.

~ mara
Mara: So you're the crater. Sit down. Have you eaten? Is she feeding you, or was it the stew again?
Kaelen: It was the stew.
Mara: Course it was. Here. Don't argue, I've already decided.
Kaelen: Thank you. Really.
Mara: Thank me by not falling over in my doorway.
set ch1_mara_met

~ farmers
Tull: Water doesn't go uphill, Wenna.
Wenna: Then go and tell it, because it's halfway up my bean rows.
Tull: You left the sluice open again.
Wenna: I've never left a sluice open in my life.
Tull: The spring of the flood.
Wenna: That was the sluice's fault.

~ lost_sword
Child: Have you seen my sword? It's wood. It's a good one.
Kaelen: What does it look like?
Child: Like a sword.
Kaelen: ...Right. I'll keep an eye out.

~ lost_sword_found_pickup
Kaelen (Internal): A wooden sword. Good one, too.

~ lost_sword_found
Child: You found it! Are you a knight?
Kaelen: No. I just look like I lost a fight with one.
Child: My uncle Aldric's a knight. He's away.
set ch1_child_sword_returned

# ── Free roam: repeat visits, the shop, the market stone, Bran's post ─────

~ mara_repeat
Mara: Back again? Good. Buy something or carry something, love. Pick one.

~ whispering_stone
Kaelen: What is this thing?
Elara: The Whispering Stone. Prices, mostly.
Kaelen (Internal): Numbers crawling up a rock. Grain in Ironhold, iron in places I've never heard of. It's a live market feed, carved into stone.
Kaelen: Does anybody actually use it?
Elara: Rook does, when he comes through. Everyone else just argues with it.
set ch1_auction_house_visited

~ whispering_stone_repeat
Kaelen (Internal): Bread's up two coppers since this morning.

~ bran_repeat_field
Bran: North field first, lad. Then we'll talk about roads.

~ bran_repeat_road
Bran: Bridge is south. Have a look at it before you go anywhere.

# Data Vision secret under Bran's gatepost.
~ guard_post_secret
System: TRACE: EVACUATION_RIGHTS.CLAUSE — DISABLED.
Kaelen (Internal): Someone switched off a rule about leaving. A long time ago. Right under Bran's gatepost.

~ elara_repeat
Elara: Go on, have a look around. I'll be here, pretending I'm not watching you.
